<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Kafka Pulse: Default Partitioning</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif; background: #f4f7f6; color: #333; padding: 20px; max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; }
    h1, h2 { color: #2c3e50; }
    
    /* Concept Summary Block */
    .summary { background: #e8f4f8; border-left: 5px solid #3498db; padding: 15px 20px; border-radius: 5px; margin-bottom: 30px; }
    .summary ul { margin: 10px 0 0 0; padding-left: 20px; }
    .summary li { margin-bottom: 8px; line-height: 1.5; font-size: 15px; }

    /* Layout Grids - 3 Columns for Phase 1 */
    .row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 15px; margin-bottom: 30px; }
    
    /* Box Styles */
    .box { background: white; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.05); }
    .box h3 { margin-top: 0; text-align: center; color: #34495e; border-bottom: 2px solid #ecf0f1; padding-bottom: 10px; font-size: 16px; }
    
    /* Messages & Highlights */
    .msg { background: #f9f9f9; border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 14px; font-family: monospace; }
    .msg.highlight { background: #fff3cd; border-color: #ffeeba; border-left: 4px solid #ffc107; font-weight: bold; }
    
    /* UI Elements */
    button { background: #3498db; color: white; border: none; padding: 10px 20px; font-size: 16px; border-radius: 5px; cursor: pointer; transition: 0.2s; margin-bottom: 20px; }
    button:hover { background: #2980b9; }
    button:disabled { background: #bdc3c7; cursor: not-allowed; }
    .assigned-label { text-align: center; color: #7f8c8d; font-size: 13px; margin-top: -10px; margin-bottom: 15px; font-weight: bold; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <h1>Feature 1: The Basics - Default No-Key Partitioning</h1>
  
  <div class="summary">
    <h2>Concept Summary</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>In Kafka, a <strong>Topic</strong> is just a logical grouping of messages.</li>
      <li>Inside a Topic, messages are stored in <strong>Partitions</strong>, which reside on physical or virtual servers where data is stored.</li>
      <li>strong>Brokers</strong> are the physical or virtual servers where data resides.</li>
      <li><strong>Producers</strong> produce messages and <strong>Consumers</strong> consume them.</li>
      <li>In Kafka, every message consists of a Key and a Value.</li>
      <li>If a message has <strong>no key</strong>, Kafka uses its Default Partitioning Strategy.</li>
      <li>We created a new Topic "DefaultPartitioning" with 1 Producer and 3 Consumers.</li>
      <li>The topic is configured with <strong>3 Partitions</strong>.</li>
      <li>Right now, we pass <strong>no key</strong> in our messages.</li>
      <li>In its simplest conceptual form, it distributes messages to partitions in a <strong>Round-Robin</strong> fashion.</li>
      <li>1st goes to Partition 1, 2nd to Partition 2, 3rd to Partition 3, and then back to 1.</li>
      <li>In reality, this partitioning algorithm includes performance optimizations (Sticky Partitioning).</li>
      <li>It uses a batch size (say 5): it sends the first 5 messages to the first partition, the next 5 to the next, and so on.</li>
      <li>Each Partition is assigned to only <strong>1 fixed Consumer</strong>.</li>
      <li>Each Consumer consumes messages exclusively from its fixed assigned Partition.</li>
      <li>Intuitively, Partitions are the primary mechanism to achieve <strong>concurrent processing</strong>.</li>
      <li>🚀 Go ahead and give it a try to see it in action!</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div style="text-align: center;">
    <button id="produce-btn" onclick="produce()">Produce Message (0/6)</button>
  </div>

  <h2>1. Partitions (The Storage)</h2>
  <div class="row" id="partitions-view">
    <!-- Partitions injected here via JS -->
  </div>

  <h2>2. Consumers (The Workers)</h2>
  <div class="row" id="consumers-view">
    <!-- Consumers injected here via JS -->
  </div>

  <script>
    async function produce() {
      await fetch('/default-partitioning/api/produce-message', { method: 'POST' });
      updateUI(); // Fetch immediately for snappy feedback
    }

    async function updateUI() {
      const res = await fetch('/default-partitioning/api/fetch-state');
      const state = await res.json();

      // Check how many messages have been produced
      // (Using taskCounter if your backend sends it, otherwise safely counting the arrays)
      const totalProduced = state.taskCounter !== undefined 
        ? state.taskCounter 
        : (state.partitions[0].length + state.partitions[1].length + state.partitions[2].length);

      // Update Producer Button State
      const btn = document.getElementById('produce-btn');
      if (totalProduced >= 6) {
        btn.disabled = true;
        btn.innerText = "Max Messages Reached (6/6)";
      } else {
        btn.disabled = false;
        btn.innerText = `Produce Message (${totalProduced}/6)`;
      }

      // 1. Draw the Partitions Row
      let pHTML = '';
      for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
        // If the message is the latest one, add the 'highlight' class
        let msgs = state.partitions[i].map(m => 
          `<div class="msg ${m === state.latestTask ? 'highlight' : ''}">${m}</div>`
        ).join('');
        
        pHTML += `<div class="box">
                    <h3>Partition ${i}</h3>
                    ${msgs || '<p style="text-align:center; color:#aaa; font-style:italic; font-size: 13px;">Empty</p>'}
                  </div>`;
      }
      document.getElementById('partitions-view').innerHTML = pHTML;

      // 2. Draw the Consumers Row
      let cHTML = '';
      for (let name of ["Consumer A", "Consumer B", "Consumer C"]) {
        let data = state.consumers[name];
        
        // If the message is the latest one, add the 'highlight' class here too
        let msgs = data.messages.map(m => 
          `<div class="msg ${m === state.latestTask ? 'highlight' : ''}">${m}</div>`
        ).join('');
        
        cHTML += `<div class="box">
                    <h3>${name}</h3>
                    <p class="assigned-label">Assigned Partition: ${data.partition}</p>
                    ${msgs || '<p style="text-align:center; color:#aaa; font-style:italic; font-size: 13px;">Waiting...</p>'}
                  </div>`;
      }
      document.getElementById('consumers-view').innerHTML = cHTML;
    }

    // Refresh the UI every 2 seconds
    setInterval(updateUI, 2000);
    updateUI();
  </script>
</body>
</html>